  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for Digital Media Education and Policy Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Bangladesh has requested support to allow four schoolteachers to attend a 5 day online training course on Digital Media Education and Policy Development.  The training is offered by the Catholic Media Council in cooperation with BEGECA (formerly part of Misereor) and Tulip training services.  The training is aimed at educators, youth leaders and others who are concerned about safeguarding young people in the digital space.  Issues covered include (i) digital media &amp; pastoral reflection, (ii) developing strategies for digital wellbeing, (iii) strengthening digital security and cybersecurity, (iv) empowering youth with critical online thinking skills, (v) identifying fake news &amp; fact checking, (vi) enhancing cybersecurity defences for digital safety, (vii) the role of artificial intelligence in media education, (viii) media education &amp; safeguarding youth.</narrative>
  </description>
